Subject: [PATCH] config: read /etc/daynight.state sidecar as the day/night source of truth
Target: prudynt-t @ f4b32289359d176fb0795d9f3735af0bd9d6d2fd (stacks on 0001-0014)

The two MQTT-frequent modes (auto/day/night) used to persist as daynight.enabled
+ daynight.force_mode inside /etc/prudynt.json, so every toggle rewrote the whole
~8.5 KB file (jffs2 wear) through a non-atomic jct write. They now persist in a
tiny, atomically-written sidecar /etc/daynight.state ("mode=auto|day|night").

CFG::load() reads that sidecar at config-load and derives daynight.enabled +
daynight.force_mode_cfg from it, AFTER the prudynt.json item loops (so it
overrides them) and UNCONDITIONALLY of jsonConfig: the sidecar is a SEPARATE
file, so if a power cut truncates prudynt.json (0012 then applies factory
defaults) the surviving sidecar still restores the persisted mode. A missing /
unreadable / unrecognized sidecar falls back to auto (the safe default); prudynt
never reads the legacy prudynt.json daynight keys once a one-time migration has
created the sidecar (the rootfs runs `daynight-state migrate` before launch).
Because IMPSystem::init() (patch 0001) derives the ISP running_mode from
force_mode_cfg BEFORE the pipeline is built, setting it here makes a forced
colour/mono mode actually stick on the sc2336p; there is no late boot re-apply.

The sidecar is read with plain C stdio (fopen/fgets) -- NOT std::ifstream:
constructing a C++ filebuf at this point segfaults inside the T23 uClibc compat
shim (libuclibcshim). fopen is the same primitive libjct and OSD.cpp use. The
strdup is strcmp-guarded (CFG::load re-runs on every prudynt.json reload via
ConfigWatcher and force_mode_cfg is never freed). The parser skips a leading
quote + any whitespace, identical to the rootfs helper, so prudynt and the shell
can never disagree.

Two hunks (the <cstdio> include + the CFG::load block); uses <cstdio>/<cstring>/
<string>. Verified: git apply --check AND patch -p1 --dry-run both pass against
f4b3228 + 0001-0014.

diff --git a/src/Config.cpp b/src/Config.cpp
index 5861a39..e42a157 100644
--- a/src/Config.cpp
+++ b/src/Config.cpp
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cmath>
 #include <cstdint>
+#include <cstdio>
 #include <filesystem>
 #include <fstream>
 #include <functional>
@@ -1400,6 +1401,57 @@ void CFG::load() {
     }
   }
 
+  // 0015: /etc/daynight.state is the single source of truth for the two
+  // MQTT-frequent day/night keys (daynight.enabled + daynight.force_mode). It is
+  // a tiny sidecar written atomically by the rootfs helper `daynight-state`, so
+  // toggling auto/day/night no longer rewrites the whole ~8.5KB prudynt.json.
+  // Apply it AFTER the prudynt.json item loops (so it overrides them) and
+  // UNCONDITIONALLY -- even when jsonConfig is null because the main config was
+  // corrupt/truncated and 0012 fell back to defaults. The sidecar is a SEPARATE
+  // file that survives a prudynt.json truncation, so honoring it here is exactly
+  // the power-outage recovery we want. Format: one line "mode=auto|day|night";
+  // a missing / unreadable / unrecognized sidecar => auto (safe default). prudynt
+  // never consults the legacy prudynt.json keys once a migration has created the
+  // sidecar (S31prudynt runs `daynight-state migrate` before launch). Because
+  // IMPSystem::init() derives running_mode (color/mono) from force_mode_cfg
+  // BEFORE the pipeline is built (patch 0001), setting it here is what makes the
+  // persisted mode stick on this sensor -- there is no late boot-script re-apply.
+  {
+    // Read the sidecar with plain C stdio (fopen/fgets), NOT std::ifstream:
+    // constructing a C++ filebuf here -- the first one in the process -- segfaults
+    // inside the uClibc compat shim on this T23 build. fopen is the same primitive
+    // libjct and OSD.cpp use successfully. Parse "mode=auto|day|night" from the
+    // first line, skipping a leading quote/whitespace, identical to the rootfs
+    // helper's sed so prudynt and the shell can never disagree on a value.
+    char scbuf[64];
+    scbuf[0] = '\0';
+    if (FILE *scf = fopen("/etc/daynight.state", "r")) {
+      if (!fgets(scbuf, sizeof(scbuf), scf))
+        scbuf[0] = '\0';
+      fclose(scf);
+    }
+    std::string scMode;
+    if (const char *mp = std::strstr(scbuf, "mode=")) {
+      mp += 5;
+      while (*mp == '"' || *mp == ' ' || *mp == '\t' || *mp == '\r' ||
+             *mp == '\n' || *mp == '\f' || *mp == '\v')
+        ++mp;
+      while (*mp >= 'a' && *mp <= 'z')
+        scMode.push_back(*mp++);
+    }
+    // Map to the two config members. strdup ONLY on an actual change: CFG::load()
+    // re-runs on every prudynt.json reload (ConfigWatcher), and force_mode_cfg is
+    // never freed, so an unconditional strdup would leak the prior string each
+    // reload -- mirror the 0013 / JSON-API strcmp-guard discipline. "auto" /
+    // missing / corrupt / unrecognized => enabled + empty force_mode (safe default).
+    const char *want =
+        (scMode == "day") ? "day" : (scMode == "night") ? "night" : "";
+    daynight.enabled = (want[0] == '\0');
+    if (!daynight.force_mode_cfg ||
+        std::strcmp(daynight.force_mode_cfg, want) != 0)
+      daynight.force_mode_cfg = strdup(want);
+  }
+
   if (!daynight.loglevel || daynight.loglevel[0] == '\0') {
     daynight.loglevel = (general.loglevel && general.loglevel[0] != '\0')
                             ? general.loglevel
